1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means the Accessibility Mod Manager application, including all
   source code, binaries, documentation, and associated files in this
   repository.

   "Security Mechanisms" means all code and functionality related to plugin
   registry signature verification, SHA256 package verification, zip-slip
   prevention, manifest action allowlisting, receipt tamper detection, plugin
   collision detection, HTTPS enforcement, and any other security or integrity
   checks present in the Software.

   "Plugin Content" means any mod packages, plugin repository indexes, game
   definitions, or other content authored and distributed by plugin authors
   through the Software's plugin system.

   "Official Distribution" means the Software as distributed by the copyright
   holders through official channels (GitHub releases, official website, or
   other channels designated by the copyright holders).

2. PERMITTED USES

   You may:

   a) View, read, and study the source code for personal, educational, or
      security auditing purposes.

   b) Submit contributions (pull requests, bug reports, patches) to the
      official repository, subject to the project's contribution guidelines.

   c) Build the Software from source for personal use, provided no
      modifications are made to Security Mechanisms.

   d) Create plugins and plugin content that integrate with the Software's
      plugin system as intended.

3. RESTRICTIONS

   You may NOT:

   a) Remove, disable, weaken, bypass, or modify any Security Mechanisms,
      whether in source or binary form.

   b) Distribute modified versions of the Software, in source or binary form,
      without prior written permission from the copyright holders.

   c) Distribute unmodified copies of the Software outside of linking to or
      directing users to the Official Distribution.

   d) Use the Software's source code, in whole or in part, to create a
      competing or derivative application.

   e) Use the Software to circumvent, bypass, or undermine protections that
      plugin authors have placed on their Plugin Content, including but not
      limited to access controls, distribution restrictions, or licensing
      terms.

   f) Redistribute, rehost, mirror, or repackage Plugin Content obtained
      through the Software without explicit permission from the respective
      plugin author.

   g) Use the Software or its source code for any purpose that would harm
      the safety, security, or accessibility of end users.

